From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] test: run the DebugInfo llc tests for x86_64 on every host

The DebugInfo tests run llc with %triple, the default target triple, on IR
translated back from SPIR-V, which keeps the SPIR calling conventions. Only
the X86 backend accepts those (as the C convention); on an AArch64 host 39
tests abort with "LLVM ERROR: unsupported calling convention". Use x86_64
whenever llc has the X86 backend.
---
--- a/test/DebugInfo/lit.local.cfg
+++ b/test/DebugInfo/lit.local.cfg
@@ -1,4 +1,21 @@
-config.substitutions.append(('%triple', config.target_triple))
+import os
+import subprocess
+
+# The reverse-translated IR keeps the SPIR calling conventions (spir_func,
+# spir_kernel). The X86 backend lowers them like the C convention, but other
+# backends (AArch64, ...) stop with "LLVM ERROR: unsupported calling
+# convention", so on those hosts every llc run below failed. Run llc for
+# x86_64 whenever it has the X86 backend; the default triple otherwise.
+def _llc_has_x86():
+    try:
+        out = subprocess.run([os.path.join(config.llvm_tools_dir, 'llc'), '--version'],
+                             capture_output=True, text=True).stdout
+    except OSError:
+        return False
+    return any(line.split()[:1] == ['x86-64'] for line in out.splitlines())
+
+config.substitutions.append(('%triple', 'x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu' if _llc_has_x86()
+                             else config.target_triple))
 
 # Building all dependencies for debug info tests takes too long,
 # so CI terminates the build after time out.
